# Copy to .env for LOCAL runs:  cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored. This repo is public -- never commit the real one.
#
# NOTE: nothing in the harness reads .env by itself. Either export these into
# your shell, or pass the file explicitly with runner.py --env-file. Be aware
# that promptfoo loads --env-file AFTER the ambient environment and OVERRIDES
# an already-exported PROMPTFOO_CONFIG_DIR, which is why gate.yml refuses to
# run when eval/.env.ci sets that key.

# The provider under test. Only needed once eval/promptfooconfig.yaml calls a
# real model -- the placeholder file://provider.py needs no key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI does NOT read this file. These go in GitHub repo secrets, at
# Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret:
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY        required once the suite calls a real model
#   DRIFT_HEARTBEAT_URL   optional. A ping URL from any free cron-monitoring
#                         service (healthchecks.io, cronitor, Better Stack).
#                         Create a check with period 1 day and grace ~6h, then
#                         paste its ping URL. It is the ONLY thing that can
#                         notice GitHub disabling the nightly schedule, because
#                         the in-repo dead-man's switch is itself a step of the
#                         workflow that would have stopped running. Leave it
#                         unset and the nightly warns instead of failing.
